From 077ccbe8b91db8e60d78fb522a9acec53170a3cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Hertel <mail@christopher-hertel.de>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:50:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [MCP Bundle] Add `session.lock` to serialize the requests of
 one session

mcp/sdk 0.9 adds an opt-in per-session lock, `Builder::setSessionLock()`, so two
requests of one session running at the same time cannot overwrite each other's
session changes (modelcontextprotocol/php-sdk#584).

`session.lock` exposes it per server, off by default like in the SDK. Next to the
`file` store it is a `FileSessionLock` in the same directory; any other store
needs `factory`, a `LockFactory` service, and gets a `SymfonyLockSessionLock`
prefixed per server. A shared store without a factory is rejected, since a file
lock would only serialize the requests that land on one machine.
